      "referenceAnswer": {
       "blocks": [
        {
         "type": "markdown",
         "value": "Learning and practice are closely connected. Learning gives us theories, methods and correct directions, while practice helps us test what we have learned in real situations. Without learning, practice may become blind. Without practice, learning may stay on paper. In my opinion, students should balance the two. We should learn carefully in class, read more useful materials and build a solid foundation. At the same time, we should apply knowledge through exercises, communication and real tasks. Only when learning and practice support each other can we improve efficiently and truly master English. Therefore, to succeed, we should not choose one and give up the other. We should learn in order to practice better, and practice in order to understand learning more deeply."
        }
       ]
      }
